<title>NORWAY: Statoil mulls Vietnam LPG plant.</title>
<headline>Statoil mulls Vietnam LPG plant.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday it was considering opportunities for importing liquefied petroleum gas (LPG) to Vietnam's Can Tho province in the Mekong delta.</p>
<p>The company's Status Weekly newsletter said Statoil Asia Pacific in Singapore also was considering building a plant to bottle LPG.</p>
<p>LPG, comprising propane and butane, are important household products in the Vietnamese market and are primarily used for cooking. THe Mekong delta has some 17 million people, Statoil said.</p>
<p>-- Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
